  "notes": "The 9th Wonder school, and the research states its rule as a mix instruction: drums are \"placed with light swing and comparatively soft transients so the soul loop dominates\". Both halves are authored. Light swing is 0.54 — below the archetype's 0.58 and the lowest swung setting on this axis — and soft transients are a `velocityTiers` override at 92–108 / 68–80 / 34–44, with the hats pulled to 0.6–0.8. That subordination is the point: the melody keeps a normal density (3–7) but the kit gets out of its way. The chop school also shows in the harmony — i–iv and ii–v–i share top weight, and I–vi is authored because the research names gospel flips specifically. The bass \"follows the chop's root motion\", which is `independent_riff` at 0.72: freer than a kick-mirror, tighter than a walking line. ⚠ `confidence` is medium; the research rates it medium-high on an artist interview plus a documented producer workflow, neither of which gives numbers. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are the velocity-tier values and `swing.amount` — \"light\" and \"soft\" are directions, and 0.54 and 92–108 are this author's reading of them. `percs.gainOffsetDb` −9 is the same inference by another route.",
